WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.090 --> 00:00:01.710
- Do you use a fake Starbucks name?

00:00:01.710 --> 00:00:03.000
- I do not actually.

00:00:03.000 --> 00:00:04.180
- Why, what's your name?

00:00:04.180 --> 00:00:05.013
- Zack.

00:00:05.013 --> 00:00:05.846
So, it's pretty easy.

00:00:05.846 --> 00:00:06.679
- Oh, my God!

00:00:06.679 --> 00:00:08.450
That's my fake Starbucks name!

00:00:09.640 --> 00:00:11.000
Is that really your fake Starbucks name?

00:00:11.000 --> 00:00:11.833
- No.

00:00:11.833 --> 00:00:14.500
(upbeat music)

00:00:14.500 --> 00:00:15.850
- Hi, my name is Amal,

00:00:15.850 --> 00:00:17.490
and I make videos at Buzzfeed.

00:00:17.490 --> 00:00:19.370
Now, I know what you're thinking.

00:00:19.370 --> 00:00:21.014
That girl has a weird name.

00:00:21.014 --> 00:00:24.020
She probably uses a fake name
when she goes to Starbucks.

00:00:24.020 --> 00:00:24.853
I don't.

00:00:24.853 --> 00:00:26.440
But some of you know the drill.

00:00:26.440 --> 00:00:27.300
You get in line,

00:00:27.300 --> 00:00:28.810
about to order your favorite drink,

00:00:28.810 --> 00:00:31.143
and you pull out your trusty fake name.

00:00:31.143 --> 00:00:32.930
You know, the classics.

00:00:32.930 --> 00:00:35.573
John, Carl, or my personal favorite,

00:00:35.573 --> 00:00:36.970
Gertrude.

00:00:36.970 --> 00:00:39.540
Today, we'll see what your
favorite Buzzfeeders use

00:00:39.540 --> 00:00:41.440
as their fake names when
they go to Starbucks.

00:00:41.440 --> 00:00:43.760
All to avoid social interaction.

00:00:43.760 --> 00:00:44.670
Let's go!

00:00:44.670 --> 00:00:45.820
What's your fake name?

00:00:45.820 --> 00:00:46.653
- K.

00:00:46.653 --> 00:00:47.486
- And what's your real name?

00:00:47.486 --> 00:00:48.350
- Kuwilileni.

00:00:48.350 --> 00:00:50.880
K because if I ever
tried to say Kuwilileni,

00:00:50.880 --> 00:00:53.030
they would just look at
me with their mouth agape

00:00:53.030 --> 00:00:54.320
like who?

00:00:54.320 --> 00:00:55.153
What?

00:00:55.153 --> 00:00:55.986
Where?

00:00:55.986 --> 00:00:57.660
- My fake name is Horchata Jose.

00:00:57.660 --> 00:00:59.090
My real name is Sergio.

00:00:59.090 --> 00:01:00.640
- My fake name is David.

00:01:00.640 --> 00:01:01.780
- And what's your real name?

00:01:01.780 --> 00:01:02.613
- Armand.

00:01:02.613 --> 00:01:04.650
My real name is on my credit card,

00:01:04.650 --> 00:01:05.900
and nobody has been like, hey!

00:01:05.900 --> 00:01:07.313
This doesn't match.

00:01:07.313 --> 00:01:09.520
- Well, you're now exposed, so...

00:01:09.520 --> 00:01:10.420
- Oh, c'mon!

00:01:10.420 --> 00:01:13.440
- If I wanna have, like fun,
I'll use like Axel Foley

00:01:13.440 --> 00:01:14.510
or like Theo Huxtable.

00:01:14.510 --> 00:01:16.120
- You seem like a Theo to me.

00:01:16.120 --> 00:01:17.640
- My fake name is Kelly.

00:01:17.640 --> 00:01:18.860
- And what's your real name?

00:01:18.860 --> 00:01:20.540
- Kirby, like the video game.

00:01:20.540 --> 00:01:21.790
The pink, little pink ball.

00:01:21.790 --> 00:01:22.724
- Okay, what's your fake name?

00:01:22.724 --> 00:01:24.260
- Lauren.

00:01:24.260 --> 00:01:25.105
- And what's your real name?

00:01:25.105 --> 00:01:27.160
- My real name is Selorm.

00:01:27.160 --> 00:01:30.030
My name is actually supposed
to be pronounced, "sellum".

00:01:30.030 --> 00:01:33.690
- So, your real name is your fake name?

00:01:33.690 --> 00:01:35.910
Ken, do you have a fake name
when you go to Starbucks?

00:01:35.910 --> 00:01:37.796
- My fake name is actually Ken.

00:01:37.796 --> 00:01:38.710
(dramatic gong)

00:01:38.710 --> 00:01:41.349
So, I moved to the states
when I was 12 or 13,

00:01:41.349 --> 00:01:44.800
and I still went by my
real name which is Kyohei.

00:01:44.800 --> 00:01:46.951
- Well, thanks for lying to
me for all these years, Ken.

00:01:46.951 --> 00:01:48.974
- I've only known you for
three months, but okay.

00:01:48.974 --> 00:01:49.807
(record scratching)

00:01:49.807 --> 00:01:50.990
- What's your fake name?

00:01:50.990 --> 00:01:51.823
- Bob.

00:01:51.823 --> 00:01:53.120
(both laughing)

00:01:53.120 --> 00:01:54.470
My real name is Onyinyechukwu.

00:01:54.470 --> 00:01:55.660
- So, don't take this the wrong way,

00:01:55.660 --> 00:01:57.970
but you're not giving me Bob vibes.

00:01:57.970 --> 00:01:59.366
- They know I'm not a Bob, but it's like,

00:01:59.366 --> 00:02:01.040
it's an understanding.

00:02:01.040 --> 00:02:03.290
They appreciate that I'm
not wasting their time.

00:02:03.290 --> 00:02:04.310
They're not wasting my time.

00:02:04.310 --> 00:02:06.530
- I will give any J name.

00:02:06.530 --> 00:02:09.490
I'll say John, Jamiroquai,

00:02:09.490 --> 00:02:12.640
Jacob, or JoMariePayton
as one word just to see.

00:02:12.640 --> 00:02:14.290
My real name is Jarrett.

00:02:14.290 --> 00:02:17.170
And they've spelled it
so wrong, so many times

00:02:17.170 --> 00:02:18.930
that I started a hashtag on my Instagram.

00:02:18.930 --> 00:02:19.970
- What's your fake name?

00:02:19.970 --> 00:02:21.000
- Dilly Dilly.

00:02:21.000 --> 00:02:21.912
- And your real name?

00:02:21.912 --> 00:02:23.610
- Danny Rosenberg.

00:02:23.610 --> 00:02:25.740
- So, instead of making
it easier for them,

00:02:25.740 --> 00:02:27.880
you're actually making it harder for them.

00:02:27.880 --> 00:02:28.713
- A little bit.

00:02:28.713 --> 00:02:29.670
I like to spice up their day.

00:02:29.670 --> 00:02:30.850
You know, they have to say a lot of names.

00:02:30.850 --> 00:02:34.290
So, yelling out, Dilly Dilly,
is kind of, I don't know...

00:02:34.290 --> 00:02:35.820
- Well, there you have it folks.

00:02:35.820 --> 00:02:36.653
The good.

00:02:36.653 --> 00:02:37.486
The bad.

00:02:37.486 --> 00:02:38.319
And the awkward.

00:02:38.319 --> 00:02:39.605
Do you use a fake name at Starbucks?

00:02:39.605 --> 00:02:40.663
Let us know.

00:02:40.663 --> 00:02:42.350
I'm gonna get some coffee.

00:02:43.710 --> 00:02:46.520
How does it feel like to
be a fake Starbucks name?

00:02:46.520 --> 00:02:49.230
- Oh, Zack is a popular name?

00:02:49.230 --> 00:02:50.081
- I mean, sure.

00:02:50.081 --> 00:02:50.914
- You know?

00:02:50.914 --> 00:02:52.080
I kinda like that actually.

00:02:52.080 --> 00:02:53.730
People are like trying to be me.

00:02:53.730 --> 00:02:55.150
Trying to use my name.

00:02:56.035 --> 00:02:58.159
(metallic screeching and squeaking)

